Chapter 11: Explain why creating tests can be useful in the process of software development.

    Writing tests can be helpful in many ways when the process of software development is underway. When using tests, you can be more confident that your code will work as
intended when used by more and more people. Tests allow you to evaluate new additions to your code to make certain that whatever you're changing doesn't break your existing 
program. Mistakes will happen during software development, so it is important that tests allow you to catch problems before they cause issues for users of the program.
Tests also, when well-written, act as a form of self-documenting code. By listing the expected inputs, outputs, and behavior, tests make the program easier to understand
and maintain. Another benefit of using tests is that it encourages the development of clean and more modular code as well as increases the developers' confidence in making
changes, knowing that any possible problems and errors will be caught by the test.
